# Phase 4.5 test fixtures are byte-exact documents. Git must not touch them.
#
# This file exists because of a bug that would only have appeared on someone
# else's machine. `git add` reported "LF will be replaced by CRLF" for
# tests/Jobkeep.Tests/Fixtures/resume.pdf — git's binary heuristic looks for NUL
# bytes in the first block, and a small hand-built PDF is almost entirely ASCII,
# so git classified it as text and offered to convert its line endings.
#
# For a PDF that is corruption, not a formatting preference. A PDF's trailing
# xref table stores the **byte offset** of every object; rewriting LF to CRLF
# shifts every one of those offsets and the file stops parsing. It would have
# passed here, where the working copy is the original, and failed on a fresh
# clone and in CI on Linux — the worst shape of bug to leave behind.
#
# The .docx and .doc fixtures were already detected as binary (they contain NUL
# bytes) but are listed anyway: relying on a heuristic that has already been
# wrong once for the same directory is not a decision, it is luck.
tests/Jobkeep.Tests/Fixtures/*.pdf   binary
tests/Jobkeep.Tests/Fixtures/*.docx  binary
tests/Jobkeep.Tests/Fixtures/*.doc   binary

# resume.txt is deliberately NOT marked binary. It is a text fixture, the
# extractor normalises line endings as its first job, and there is a test that
# pins exactly that — so a checkout that changes its EOLs is a case worth
# exercising rather than one to suppress.
